        <div class="twelve-prose">
          <h2>12th Pass Government Jobs 2026</h2>
          <p>
            After completing 12th (Higher Secondary / 10+2), candidates become eligible for a wide range of government jobs in India. From <strong>SSC CHSL</strong> and <strong>SSC Stenographer</strong> to <strong>Delhi Police Constable</strong>, <strong>BSF Head Constable</strong>, <strong>Indian Navy Agniveer SSR</strong>, and <strong>Indian Air Force Agniveer Vayu</strong> — there are hundreds of 12th pass level vacancies announced every year across central, state, defence, and railway departments.
          </p>

          <h2>Latest 12th Pass Government Job Vacancies</h2>
          <p>
            The table above lists all currently open 12th pass government jobs with real vacancy numbers, last dates, and official apply links. Jobs are updated regularly as new notifications are released by SSC, UPSC, Railway, CAPFs, and state governments.
          </p>

          <h2>12th Pass Govt Job Online Form</h2>
          <p>
            Most 12th pass government jobs now accept online applications. Candidates need to register on the official portal (ssc.nic.in for SSC, joinindiannavy.gov.in for Navy, rrbcdg.gov.in for Railway, etc.), fill the form, upload documents, and pay the fee online. Always apply through the official website — never through third-party portals.
          </p>

          <h2>12th Pass Govt Jobs — Salary & Pay Scale</h2>
          <p>
            Salary for 12th pass government jobs varies by post and pay level:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>SSC CHSL LDC:</strong> Rs. 19,900–63,200 (Pay Level-2)</li>
            <li><strong>SSC CHSL DEO:</strong> Rs. 25,500–81,100 (Pay Level-4)</li>
            <li><strong>BSF/CISF/CRPF Head Constable:</strong> Rs. 25,500–81,100 (Pay Level-4)</li>
            <li><strong>BSF/CISF ASI Steno:</strong> Rs. 29,200–92,300 (Pay Level-5)</li>
            <li><strong>Delhi Police Head Constable Ministerial:</strong> Rs. 25,500–81,100 (Pay Level-4)</li>
            <li><strong>RRB NTPC UG:</strong> Rs. 19,900–63,200 (Pay Level-2 to 3)</li>
            <li><strong>Agniveer (Navy/Air Force/Army):</strong> Rs. 30,000–40,000 monthly stipend</li>
            <li><strong>UPSC NDA:</strong> Rs. 56,100 (Level-10) during training</li>
          </ul>
          <p>All posts include Dearness Allowance (DA), House Rent Allowance (HRA), Transport Allowance, Medical Benefits, and pension under NPS/GPS.</p>

          <h2>Eligibility for 12th Pass Government Jobs</h2>
          <p>
            The basic eligibility for 12th pass government jobs is passing 10+2 from a recognized board. Some posts require specific subjects:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Any stream:</strong> SSC CHSL, Delhi Police Constable, BSF HC, SSC Stenographer</li>
            <li><strong>12th Science (Physics + Maths):</strong> Indian Air Force Agniveer Vayu, NDA (Air Force/Navy), Indian Coast Guard Navik GD</li>
            <li><strong>12th Science (Physics + Chemistry + Maths):</strong> Indian Navy SSR/AA</li>
            <li><strong>With Typing:</strong> Delhi Police HC Ministerial, BSF HC Ministerial, CRPF HC Ministerial</li>
            <li><strong>With Shorthand:</strong> BSF ASI Steno, CISF ASI Steno</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Age Limit</h2>
          <p>
            Age limits vary by recruiting body. The general range is 18–27 years for SSC exams, 18–25 for CAPF/Police, 17–23 for Agniveer, and 18–30 for Railway. Age relaxation is provided as per government rules: SC/ST — 5 years, OBC — 3 years, PwD — 10 years, Ex-servicemen — as per rules. Use the <a href="/tools/age-calculator/" style="color:var(--saffron)">Age Calculator</a> to check your eligibility.
          </p>

          <h2>Selection Process</h2>
          <p>
            The selection process for 12th pass government jobs typically includes:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>SSC CHSL:</strong> Tier-1 (CBT) → Tier-2 (CBT + Descriptive) → Tier-3 (Skill/Typing Test) → Document Verification</li>
            <li><strong>Delhi Police Constable:</strong> CBT → Physical Endurance & Measurement Test → Medical Exam</li>
            <li><strong>BSF/CRPF Head Constable:</strong> CBT → Physical Standard Test → Medical Exam</li>
            <li><strong>Indian Navy SSR/AA:</strong> CBT → Physical Fitness Test → Medical Exam</li>
            <li><strong>Agniveer Vayu:</strong> Online Test → Physical Fitness Test → Adaptability Test → Medical Exam</li>
            <li><strong>RRB NTPC UG:</strong> CBT-1 → CBT-2 → Skill Test (if applicable) → Document Verification</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>State-wise 12th Pass Govt Jobs</h2>
          <p>
            Candidates looking for state-specific 12th pass jobs can explore:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="/states/rajasthan/" style="color:var(--saffron)">Rajasthan</a> — Rajasthan Police Constable, RSSB various posts</li>
